      "created_at": "2025-08-17T11:56:58.772Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hello Team,</p>\n<p>While trying to submit a <strong>Journal Entry</strong>, I encountered an error message:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Debit and Credit not equal for Journal Entry <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#ACC-JV-2025-21118</span>. Difference is 0.024.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>However, when reviewing the entry, the totals are actually equal:</p>\n<p>Total Debit: 0.300 + 0.030 = 0.330<br>\nTotal Credit: 0.330</p>\n<ul>\n<li>This looks like a <strong>rounding or precision issue</strong> with floating-point values in the Journal Entry validation.</li>\n<li>I’m using ERPNext v14.39.0</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Could you please check if this is a known bug or advise on a workaround/fix?</p>\n<p>Thank you.<br>\n<div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/8/5/855c6357685d73657ff208054fb7a33024d36437.png\" data-download-href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/855c6357685d73657ff208054fb7a33024d36437\" title=\"Screenshot 2025-08-17 140009\"><img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/8/5/855c6357685d73657ff208054fb7a33024d36437_2_690x285.png\" alt=\"Screenshot 2025-08-17 140009\" data-base62-sha1=\"j1LrwXL9C9ha8Zpoyf7oUFaCx5J\" width=\"690\" height=\"285\" srcset=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/8/5/855c6357685d73657ff208054fb7a33024d36437_2_690x285.png, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/8/5/855c6357685d73657ff208054fb7a33024d36437_2_1035x427.png 1.5x, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/8/5/855c6357685d73657ff208054fb7a33024d36437_2_1380x570.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"989B9E\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">Screenshot 2025-08-17 140009</span><span class=\"informations\">1887×781 82.6 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></p>",
